        "parms": "# ~+ ~- ~* ~/ ~clip — signal arithmetic\nThese work sample by sample on a signal in the left inlet. The right operand is a second signal, or a number used while no signal is connected there: the argument, or an int or float sent in. ~+ and ~- default to 0 (since libYSE 3.0.1), ~* and ~/ to 1. ~clip keeps every sample between a low and a high, -1 and 1 by default.\nMax writes these +~, -~, *~ and /~, and adds up every cable that reaches a signal inlet. Here the ~ comes first, and a signal inlet takes one cable: mix with a chain of ~+.",
